# i18n & document direction

## Defaults

- Default locale: **`fa`** (Persian). Root `<html lang>` must use `DEFAULT_LOCALE` from `~/lib/constants`.
- Default direction: **`rtl`**. Root `<html dir>` and `DirectionProvider` use `DEFAULT_DIR`.
- English (`en`) is a **supported** locale but **empty for now** — do not add English copy/strings until asked. Keep the multi-lang shape ready.

## Multi-lang (required)

- Architecture must stay locale-ready (`SUPPORTED_LOCALES`, locale → `dir` map).
- Locale `fa` → `rtl`; locale `en` → `ltr`. Never hardcode only one language forever.
- User-facing strings should eventually live in locale dictionaries; until i18n is wired, keep Persian as the only filled content.

## RTL / LTR — always when coding UI

- Prefer **logical** CSS/Tailwind: `ps`/`pe`, `ms`/`me`, `start`/`end`, `border-s`/`border-e`, `text-start`/`text-end`, `scroll-ps`/`scroll-pe`.
- Never use physical `left`/`right`/`ml`/`mr`/`pl`/`pr`/`text-left`/`text-right` for layout that should flip with direction.
- Directional icons (chevrons, arrows): flip with `rtl:` when needed.
- Mirror checks mentally for both `dir="rtl"` and `dir="ltr"`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
className="ml-4 pl-2 text-left left-0"

// ✅ GOOD
className="ms-4 ps-2 text-start start-0"
```

## Constants source of truth

Use `DEFAULT_LOCALE`, `DEFAULT_DIR`, `SUPPORTED_LOCALES`, and `LOCALE_DIR` from `~/lib/constants` — do not invent ad-hoc lang/dir strings in layouts.
